{"agent":"main","body":{"error":null,"exit":0,"for_seq":13,"result_bytes":563,"result_hash":"sha256:d2bace78cb0a6dba26a15c9c687689fe239b82f3c142f68f17bd39d635d476b3","result_inline":"1\t# slugify changelog\n2\t\n3\t## 2.0.0\n4\t\n5\tBreaking:\n6\t- `slugify(text, separator)` is now `slugify(text, options)`. Passing a string as the second argument is no longer supported.\n7\t- Lowercasing is opt-in: pass `{ lower: true }`. 1.x always lowercased.\n8\t- The default separator is `_` (was `-`).\n9\t\n10\tAdded:\n11\t- `strict: true` drops every character that is not a letter or a digit instead of turning runs of them into a separator.\n12\t\n13\t## 1.4.2\n14\t\n15\t- Combining marks are stripped after NFKD normalisation, so accented letters become their base letter.\n16\t","served":"live","truncated":false,"wall_ms":0},"hash":"sha256:f55101f58d3a96c4a9ae1bcb38a267162cdeee7be6d662ad20e1365631d259e4","mono_ns":14000000,"prev":"sha256:90dfdcc19b532131478745e47679f6fad545e8a73f29cd82e3656a1840f8f3c3","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":14,"session":"9139e412-589e-41fd-8406-759534819e7e","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.014Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_result"}
